  "body": "## Accepted complete many-one hardness result\n\nLegal chip-firing reachability is coNP-complete on finite loopless strongly\nconnected directed multigraphs with binary adjacency entries and nonnegative\nbinary-encoded initial and target configurations. Target: 3000016 /\nAMR-029-0016. The report gives the explicit polynomial-time many-one\nreduction NONHALTING <=_m REACHABLE.\n\nThe full analytic proof preserves the finite-state cutoff, gate/marker\nconstruction, exact thresholds, polynomial-bit cleanup budget, nonnegativity,\nstrong connectivity, both reduction directions, reverse proof under arbitrary\ntarget-reaching odometers, loop-removal relays and optional signed-input\nnormalization. Aggregate finite checks are supporting metadata only; the\nproof is independent of every omitted executable.\n\nSource NP-completeness is Farrell\u2013Levine, CoEulerian graphs, Corollary 3.2:\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/1502.04690 . Target coNP membership is Hujter\u2013Kiss\u2013T\u00f3thm\u00e9r\u00e9sz,\nOn the complexity of the chip-firing reachability problem, Theorem 12:\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/1507.03209 . T\u00f3thm\u00e9r\u00e9sz, Rotor-routing reachability is easy,\nchip-firing reachability is hard, Theorem 2.3,\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/2102.11970 , is a distinct prior polynomial-hierarchy\ncollapse consequence, not a substitute for the many-one reduction here.\n\n## Distribution and review limits\n\nExactly eight authored proof/audit/acceptance/status and public-source-review\nor metadata files are added under `unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/3000016/`.\nEditorial changes rename the report, reconcile the completed audit, remove\nprivate candidate and unavailable-checker references, distinguish historical\nobservations, and bind the distributed proof and audit exactly. Every\nmathematical argument, example, edge case and scope qualification remains.\n\nThis AI-assisted, unrefereed edition makes no simple-graph or unary-encoding\nhardness claim, no first-in-literature or exhaustive-current-openness claim,\nand no external human peer-review, journal-acceptance, or formal\nproof-assistant-certification claim. Programs, raw generated outputs,\ndatasets, copied third-party source bodies/PDFs/images and private\ncoordination material are excluded. Edition preparation claims no new\nscholarly retrieval, source-file rehash, source inspection, literature search,\nor mathematical test rerun.\n\nQUEUE.md and unrelated entries remain unchanged. Editorial preparation adds\nno substantive proof turn and resets no historical accounting. No merge,\nrelease, DOI or outside outreach is requested.\n\nBase commit: `f6caddda8f8be2cdb3e91494325d8f7f365bc3fc`.\n\n## Exact distributed file identities\n\n- `ACCEPTANCE.json`: 2,188 bytes; SHA-256 `b25d4890d51d0cb016584bd0361bd66be810800a420d7c2d8e94a3d6286959d1`.\n- `MANIFEST.json`: 1,600 bytes; SHA-256 `1af7e30e4e4f448da91fa05550672f6d3b8ef9264820cb0ca114ec85727c4e0d`.\n- `MATHEMATICAL_AUDIT.md`: 13,866 bytes; SHA-256 `d2fc80e04df676129fd06b3ad9036a63a4e79b81f9ae1202cee71ca4f42ab65a`.\n- `MATHEMATICAL_REPORT.md`: 9,455 bytes; SHA-256 `46f0c5c582e5775cd05628fa6dc67ede0a2f550248b84403a51bf621cbc5844c`.\n- `README.md`: 3,577 bytes; SHA-256 `dbc2237d49147f38b20e93edbc5750f3b016ef70c02945a582ffe0a976973510`.\n- `SOURCE_METADATA.json`: 5,824 bytes; SHA-256 `a96a91527c9a0c36734ac61bdfec587e0da9ace3a30189b2b8259ff6e7eaf205`.\n- `SOURCE_REVIEW.md`: 4,514 bytes; SHA-256 `073b6fa1c8a55640eb891a724b04e7669c48875f8ae5d93fda3254465df50081`.\n- `STATUS.json`: 1,693 bytes; SHA-256 `41ac12096748a13f7137d4f1f3dd687ab1bfb255e033c4efc90d6bd98b6adb1f`.\n\nThe manifest lists eight members and hashes the other seven; this body pins the manifest independently.\n",
